traceability.evidence:
Story file exists and matches the provided specification: docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md.,Rule implementation updated to support JSDoc coexistence: - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts - processCommentLine() now calls isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine and, when it returns true, finalizes any pending @story/@req annotation and stops continuation: "// Implement JSDoc tag coexistence behavior: terminate @story/@req values when a new non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g., @param, @returns) is encountered.
 // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
 if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
 finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
 return null;
 }",JSDoc tag boundary detection helper implements generic @word detection and excludes traceability tags: - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts - normalizeCommentLine() preserves line boundaries and returns lines starting from the first traceability tag when present, or strips leading '*' for other lines. - isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): - Trims leading whitespace. - Returns false if line does not start with '@'. - Returns false if it starts with @story/@req/@supports. - Returns true for any other '@' tag (e.g. @param, @returns, @throws), satisfying REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION and REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE.,Tests explicitly tied to this story and its requirements exist and pass: - tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts header: "Tests for: docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
 * @story docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md
 * @req REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE ...
 * @req REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION ...
 * @req REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION ...
 * @req REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC ...
 * @req REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES ...
 * @req REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE ...",Tests covering acceptance criteria for JSDoc coexistence: - Before other tags (REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE): - Valid case: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability before other JSDoc tags" with code placing @story/@req before @param/@returns. - After other tags (REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE): - Valid case: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability after other JSDoc tags" with @param/@returns before @story/@req. - Mixed positions (REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE, REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION, REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC): - Valid case: "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] mixed positions of traceability and other JSDoc tags" interleaving @story, @param, @req, @param, @returns. - Proper termination & no false positives (REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES): - Valid case: "[REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES] JSDoc tags do not pollute requirement ID when following @req" replicates the original bug scenario (@req followed by @param/@returns) and passes, confirming the value is not concatenated into something like "REQ-OPTIMIZATION@param{object}data". - Preserve multiline (REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE): - Valid case: "[REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE] multi-line @story annotation before other JSDoc tags" ensures multi-line @story followed by @param/@returns is still parsed correctly.,All rule tests, including the JSDoc coexistence tests for this story, are executed and passing (verbose Jest run): - From npm test output: - "PASS tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts" - Under "valid-annotation-format valid" section, the following tests pass: - "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability before other JSDoc tags" - "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] traceability after other JSDoc tags" - "[REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE] mixed positions of traceability and other JSDoc tags" - "[REQ-PRESERVE-MULTILINE] multi-line @story annotation before other JSDoc tags" - "[REQ-NO-FALSE-POSITIVES] JSDoc tags do not pollute requirement ID when following @req",Global test suite status from Jest: - "Test Suites: 1 skipped, 48 passed, 48 of 49 total" - "Tests: 2 skipped, 353 passed, 355 total" - Confirms no regressions across existing annotation parsing behavior (backward compatibility).,Documentation updated to describe JSDoc coexistence behavior, satisfying the story's documentation acceptance criterion: - docs/rules/valid-annotation-format.md, section "JSDoc coexistence": - States that traceability annotations can appear before, after, or interleaved with other JSDoc tags. - Describes that any JSDoc tag line starting with '@' (other than @story/@req/@supports) is treated as a boundary for multi-line values, and that continuation lines are only used when they don't start with another JSDoc tag. - Provides a concrete example where @story/@req coexist with @param and @returns for Story 022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.
